{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said: Let the waters swarm, etc.</b> The meaning is that creatures would form from the waters. This matter is not continuous but [occurred] only at the moment of the utterance of creation, and those creatures that the waters swarmed persisted forever, like the species of beasts that the earth brought forth — which it brought forth only at the moment of the utterance, and they persisted forever, by the command of HaShem to them, that they should swarm and be fruitful and multiply. And His saying <b>swarming creatures with a living soul</b> refers to the fish. And He used the expression שרץ to distinguish between it and the flying creature, for this one [the swarming creature] has no power except immediately adjacent to the earth, whereas the flying creature flies over the earth and does not need to be adjacent to it. It further has [the ability] to rise up to the heavens, as He says: ״עַל פְּנֵי רְקִיעַ״ — and without this utterance the birds would not have risen up to the heavens." "<b>And His saying רְקִיעַ הַשָּׁמַיִם</b> — meaning: the firmament that is called שָּׁמַיִם. And there is no difficulty according to their words, may their memory be for blessing, who said (Genesis Rabbah 6) — and this is their language: Where are the sun and the moon? In רָקִיעַ ב׳, as it is stated: ״וַיִּתֵּן אֹתָם אֱלֹהִים בִּרְקִיעַ הַשָּׁמָיִם״. The verse is full [i.e., explicit], and the Men of the Great Assembly interpreted it (Nehemiah 9:6): ״אַתָּה עָשִׂיתָ אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם וּשְׁמֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם וְכָל צְבָאָם״ — where are all their host? In רָקִיעַ ב׳, end of quote. According to their words, may their memory be for blessing, what would they answer regarding this verse: ״וְעוֹף יְעוֹפֵף עַל פְּנֵי רְקִיעַ הַשָּׁמָיִם״?" "<b>And it appears</b> that according to the vocalization, this verse differs from the verse ״וַיִּתֵּן אֹתָם״ etc. (Genesis 1:17), for here [Scripture] wrote a qamatz under the resh of רָקִיעַ, while there it wrote a sheva under the resh of רְקִיעַ. Now when He says רְקִיעַ with a sheva, it indicates that it is in construct [i.e., attached] — meaning, the firmament of the heavens. And when He says רָקִיעַ with a qamatz, it is not in construct with שָּׁמַיִם, and its meaning is: a firmament, and it is that which is called שָּׁמַיִם. With this, there is no difficulty. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:56:26.304768639Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}